[i]Version 1.7.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.7.0 ✨THE ECLIPSE: CRISIS HORROR EXPANSION✨[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ FEATURE UPDATE[/b]
[i]This patch is aimed squarely at the reports of the endgame (Aegis's mail, The Eclipse's awakening) sometimes never triggering after killing the Wormhole Guardian — plus real new content built on top once the underlying issues were found and fixed: The Eclipse now remembers who's been hunting it, whispers grow louder the deeper the crisis goes, a named horror stalks the brave (or unlucky), and a full command interface lets you check exactly where things stand at a glance. No action needed — existing saves pick up everything automatically.[/i]

[b]✨NEW FEATURES✨[/b]
[list]
[*]✨ [b]Eclipse Remembers:[/b] The more Eclipse ships you personally destroy, the more The Eclipse notices you specifically — expect more frequent, heavier personal ambushes the deeper your kill count climbs.
[*]✨ [b]The Choir:[/b] Rumors about The Eclipse grow darker and more specific as the crisis escalates — from the moment it first wakes, through full awakening, to becoming a Fallen Empire. Fly into Eclipse-held territory for the first time in a session and you'll feel it.
[*]✨ [b]The Silent Choir:[/b] A new, rare, named horror occasionally stalks a single player across the galaxy — appearing at the edge of your sensors, whispering, and vanishing before you can react. It won't do that forever.
[*]✨ [b]Ascendant Ward:[/b] A new craftable item at the Stellar Forge lets you temporarily evade The Eclipse's own hunting behavior — personal ambushes, the Silent Choir, and its shield-draining aura — for 30 minutes. Doesn't make you invisible to everyone, just to The Eclipse's own attention.
[*]✨ [b]Distress Beacon:[/b] When The Eclipse designates a Crusade against your territory, every online member of your faction or alliance now gets an alert with the target coordinates — rally your friends before it lands.
[*]✨ [b]Eclipse Wastes:[/b] Sectors The Eclipse has annihilated are no longer just foggy and guarded — they now actively drain your shields the longer you linger.
[*]✨ [b]Reclaimed Vessels:[/b] Eclipse-annihilated sectors have a small chance to spawn an Eclipse ship built from the wreckage of whoever used to hold that territory.
[*]✨ [b]The Eclipse: Command Interface:[/b] A brand-new UI window, opened by interacting with your own ship, showing everything about The Eclipse's current status at a glance — awakening progress, territory held, active threats, and your own personal standing with it — across four organized tabs.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed the Campaign Sometimes Getting Stuck With No Warning:[/b] A random-chance bug in every story mission could occasionally send you to "rendezvous coordinates" that were actually your own current sector — which meant the mission could never register you arriving, silently stalling the entire campaign with no error or message. This is fixed for good.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed a Rare Ambush/Boss Spawn Failure That Could Silently Stall a Mission:[/b] Under specific conditions, spawning an ambush fleet or a story boss could fail partway through without any warning, leaving that mission stage permanently stuck. Spawning is now verified every step of the way.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Ascendant Matter Sometimes Not Dropping Early in the Campaign:[/b] Killing Eclipse ships in the first few minutes after the Guardian's death could fail to drop Ascendant Matter, even though later kills worked fine. This resource now works correctly from the very first Eclipse ship you destroy.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Eclipse Harvesters Not Dropping Loot:[/b] Eclipse Harvester ships were never dropping their intended loot. Fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed a Crash Risk on Ascendancy Beacons and Overdrive Stations:[/b] A newly-built Ascendancy Beacon or a station with the Ascendant Overdrive system could crash on your very first interaction with it. Fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed the Ascendant Gateway Sometimes Using the Wrong Material for Defenders:[/b] The Gateway's summoned defense fleet wasn't always using the intended premium hull material. Fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed the Ascendant Aegis Reactor Erasing Other Buffs:[/b] The Aegis Reactor's Phase-Shift ability was periodically wiping out *other* temporary combat buffs on your ship instead of just managing its own. If you run other Cosmic mods, your buffs will now coexist correctly.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed a Minor Performance Hit When Ascendancy Sieges Spawn:[/b] Triggering an Ascendancy Siege event was doing more collision-avoidance work than necessary, and could very rarely nudge nearby ships that had nothing to do with the siege. Fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed a Corrupted Databank Rarity Roll:[/b] The reward rarity for Corrupted Databank stashes was rolling one tier lower than intended. Fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed the World-Eater's Doomsday Clock Sometimes Ending a Fight Early:[/b] If a fight against the World-Eater ran long, the sector could be wiped out from under you mid-battle by its own countdown, even while you were actively fighting it. The clock now stops the moment the fight actually begins — from then on, it's a fight to the finish, just like every other way you can encounter the World-Eater.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed a Rare Case of an Unkillable Eclipse Ship:[/b] Under very specific timing, an Eclipse Phantom or Interceptor's teleport-escape ability could leave it permanently invincible after a server restart or sector reload. Fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed The Eclipse Doing Nothing Visible for Hours on a Fresh Galaxy:[/b] A bug meant The Eclipse's territorial expansion (invasions, sector conquests, Crusades) could stay completely dormant for the first several hours of any new galaxy, even after the Guardian was killed and the Eclipse "awakened." This is now fixed — expansion starts on schedule.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed The Eclipse Occasionally "Re-Conquering" Its Own Territory:[/b] A rare bug could let the Eclipse's expansion counter tick up without any new ground actually changing hands, throwing off its reported progress toward becoming a Fallen Empire. Fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Some Returning Players Never Being Contacted by Aegis:[/b] Players who were away when the Guardian died, and stayed away for a while afterward, could log back in and simply never receive Aegis's contact — permanently. This is now fixed; any returning player will be caught the moment they log in.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Major Story/Threat Banners Never Actually Appearing:[/b] "THE ECLIPSE AWAKENS," Doomsday warnings, and every other dramatic on-screen banner in the mod had a bug preventing them from ever actually displaying, even though the underlying events were firing correctly. They now show up as intended.
[*]⚖️ [b]Eclipse Ship Damage/Stat Scaling Corrected:[/b] A calculation bug meant most of The Eclipse's stated percentage bonuses (fire rate, shields, speed, cargo — the ones described as "+X%" throughout their ships and abilities) were landing far weaker than intended across nearly the entire faction. This has been corrected mod-wide, so Eclipse ships now hit as hard and tank as much as their stats claim. Expect a noticeably tougher fight against Eclipse ships and bosses going forward.
[*]📖 [b]Corrected the Ascendant Gateway's Codex Description:[/b] Its in-game description didn't quite match how it actually works. Updated to be accurate.
[*]📖 [b]Translation Coverage Improved:[/b] A number of story and Eclipse-related messages that were previously always shown in English regardless of your language setting are now properly localized.
[*]📖 [b]/eclipsestatus Now Actually Tells You What's Going On:[/b] If the Eclipse hasn't fully awoken yet, the command used to say the exact same thing whether nothing had happened at all or the 10-minute awakening countdown was already ticking. It now tells you which one it actually is.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.6.2[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.6.2 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]A targeted fix for players who were still missing contact from Aegis even after the 1.6.0/1.6.1 fixes, plus a deeper safety net for the Eclipse endgame overall. No action needed on your end — existing saves will self-correct automatically.[/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Aegis Still Not Contacting Some Players:[/b] A small number of players who killed the Wormhole Guardian before the 1.6.0/1.6.1 fixes landed could still never receive Aegis's transmission or the "A Mysterious Summons" quest, even after updating and continuing to play. This is now fixed for good — affected saves will automatically pick up the missed contact the next time you're online, no reinstall or workaround needed.
[*]🐛 [b]Added a Safety Net for the Eclipse Endgame:[/b] In rare cases, a save could end up with the Eclipse fully "awakened" but missing its actual endgame systems entirely — no Eclipse faction, no territory conquest, no World-Eater. The game now automatically checks for and repairs this every few seconds, so the endgame can no longer silently fail to start.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed the Story World-Eater Not Scaling for Groups:[/b] The World-Eater you fight at the end of the campaign wasn't getting any tougher when more players or alliance members joined the fight, unlike every other version of that boss you can encounter. It now properly scales up with your group size, matching the difficulty you'd get anywhere else.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.6.1[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.6.1 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]A focused fix pass following a player-reported crash — closes a mission softlock and several other crashes found while tracking it down.[/i]

[b]📖PLAYER HINT📖[/b]
[list]
[*]📖 [b]Early Warning After Killing the Guardian:[/b] The instant you strike down the Wormhole Guardian, you'll now get an immediate hint that something is reaching out to you, about 10 seconds before Aegis's transmission actually arrives.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed The Eclipse Awakening Getting Stuck:[/b] The opening story mission could permanently get stuck right at the ambush — Eclipse ships would fail to fully spawn, the fight would never trigger, and there was no way to move the questline forward. This is now fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed a Teleport Visual Crash:[/b] Eclipse ships using their signature "Blink" teleport or Phase Shift ability could crash instead of playing their teleport effect. Both abilities now work correctly.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Ascendant Matter, Eclipse Datacores, and Ascendant Scrap Not Working:[/b] A bug meant these key crafting resources could fail to drop from Eclipse ships and Citadels, and the Ascendancy Forge, Ascendant Overdrive, and Ascendant Scrap salvage system could all fail to use them correctly. Everything involving these resources now works as intended.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Aegis Envoy Spawn Crash:[/b] Aegis's ship could crash the moment it appeared during any of the six story debriefs. Fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed a Wreckage Cleanup Error:[/b] The investigated anomaly wreck in the opening mission referenced a file that doesn't exist, causing an error during cleanup. Fixed.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.6.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.6.0 ✨FEATURE & 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!✨[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This is a big one — a full pass through the entire mod fixed the Eclipse questline getting stuck after the Guardian, Aegis not responding to you, and several boss fights not working as intended, plus four brand-new features![/i]

[b]📖 CODEX UPDATED[/b]
[list]
📖[*] Updated Cosmic Ascendancy's codex entry with up-to-date information.
[/list]

[b]✨NEW FEATURES✨[/b]
[list]
[*]✨ [b]Eclipse Threat Dashboard:[/b] /eclipsestatus now gives you the full picture: how many sectors the Eclipse holds, how close they are to their next move, whether they've gone Fallen Empire (and where they last struck), any wounded Nemesis currently on the run, and how far Remnant Escalation has climbed.
[*]✨ [b]Hunt the Dread-Lord:[/b] When a Nemesis retreats near death, it no longer just disappears for good. It flees to a nearby sector to lick its wounds, and shows up there the moment you or anyone else arrives, ready for a rematch. Finish it off for a bounty.
[*]✨ [b]Ascendancy Beacon Sanctuary Field:[/b] Upgrade your Beacon to Tier 3 or higher and it starts actively shielding the surrounding sectors from Eclipse conquest and annihilation attempts, growing to a 12-sector radius at max tier. Your ultimate defensive payoff for going all-in on a Beacon.
[*]✨ [b]Eclipse Remnant Escalation:[/b] Keep wiping out World-Eaters and Citadels, and the Eclipse's surviving remnants adapt: tougher shields, more hull, harder-hitting attacks, and a shorter fuse before the next World-Eater shows up. A long-running galaxy never plateaus.
[/list]

[b]⚖️BALANCE[/b]
[list]
[*]⚖️ [b]World-Eater Now Scales With Your Group:[/b] Fighting the World-Eater alone used to feel the same as fighting it with a full alliance backing you up. It now grows tougher shields, more hull, and harder-hitting attacks for every extra defender in the sector when it spawns, whether it's the natural Doomsday Event or one you summoned yourself with an Eclipse Datacore, so a solo fight still hits its intended difficulty and a group fight stays a real fight too. Let us know how it feels across different group sizes; the numbers may need another pass.
[*]⚖️ [b]The Eclipse Now Actually Spreads From The Core:[/b] The Eclipse was always meant to emerge from the galactic core and creep outward from there, but its actual territory-grabbing logic ignored that and could start expanding from anywhere. Their first foothold now genuinely appears near the core, and their later expansion leans outward from it over time instead of wandering completely at random.
[*]⚖️ [b]Fallen Empire Now Also Hunts Player Territory:[/b] Once the Eclipse becomes a Fallen Empire (75+ conquered sectors), it used to only ever go after AI faction homeworlds. It will now also occasionally set its sights on player and alliance sectors that have a station on them, on its own slower cooldown so it can't camp the same target back-to-back. Losing a targeted sector this way never deletes your stations, worst case it turns hostile until you clear it out.
[*]⚖️ [b]Killing a Citadel Now Actually Pushes The Eclipse Back:[/b] Destroying a Citadel used to only pause the Eclipse's expansion clock, without changing anything they already held. It now also liberates the Citadel's own sector plus nearby sectors the Eclipse controlled, rolling their territory back for real.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed the "Nothing Happens After the Guardian" Bug:[/b] Some players were killing the Wormhole Guardian, seeing the galaxy-wide warning that the Eclipse has awakened, and then... nothing. No envoy ship, no new quest. This is now fixed — the Eclipse will always properly reach out to you once it awakens, no matter how you happened to kill the Guardian.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Aegis Not Responding:[/b] Even players who did get contacted by Aegis could talk to her, click all the way through the conversation, and have nothing happen — no new mission, no rewards, stuck in a loop. This was actually the deeper bug behind the whole "questline doesn't progress" problem, and it's now fixed. Talking to Aegis will always properly advance the story and hand out your rewards.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Aegis Going Silent After Your First Chat:[/b] Even with the fix above, Aegis could still stop responding after your very first conversation with her. Every time you flew to a new rendezvous point for a debrief, she'd just sit there, never speaking to you, with no way to trigger her dialog. You can now always walk up and talk to her directly, whether or not she greets you automatically.
[*]🐛 [b]World-Eater Boss Fixes:[/b] Fixed a bug where the World-Eater could spawn with several of its core mechanics broken, including a bug that could make it drop zero loot when defeated. It will now always fight and reward you as intended, including its final "last stand" anchor pylon phase which could previously fail to trigger.
[*]🐛 [b]Elemental Resistance Fixes:[/b] Fixed several Eclipse enemies — including elite "Nemesis" ships — misreading what type of damage they were taking, which was breaking their adaptive shielding behavior.
[*]🐛 [b]Singularity Explosion Fix:[/b] Fixed a bug where a dying Singularity-class ship's death explosion could keep detonating over and over instead of just once.
[*]🐛 [b]Ascendancy Beacon Fixes:[/b] Fixed an issue where an active Beacon's sector wouldn't properly stay simulated after a dedicated server restarted, and a crash that could occur when activating a Beacon while at war (Cosmic War users only).
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Two Broken Relic Effects:[/b] The Ascendant Omni-Sensor's "Deep Scan" report and the Ascendant Slipstream Core's post-jump speed boost were both silently non-functional. Both now work as advertised.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed The Eclipse Bane Reward:[/b] This unique weapon system, rewarded for defeating the Vanguard boss, was granting none of its bonuses when installed. It now works correctly.
[*]🐛 [b]Corrected Forge Instructions:[/b] Fixed the in-game Codex entry for the Ascendancy Forge, which described the wrong item for unlocking it. It now correctly tells you to decrypt an Eclipse Datacore.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Corrupted Databank Stash Exploit & Crash:[/b] Opening one of these lore stashes had no protection against being triggered more than once, letting its loot be duplicated, and its rare "resonated" bonus stash could crash the game outright. Both are now fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed World-Eater Loot Crash:[/b] Defeating the World-Eater superboss could crash right as it tried to drop its full haul of legendary turrets and upgrades, sometimes leaving nothing behind. It will now always finish dropping its complete reward pool.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Environmental Damage Not Registering:[/b] The Eclipse Rift Stabilizer's shield-draining hazard and a Singularity-class ship's death blast were sending a malformed damage instruction to the engine, which could stop them from actually damaging nearby ships. Both now correctly deal their intended damage.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed Rare Sector Mixup During Eclipse Conquest:[/b] In specific coordinate combinations, the Eclipse's internal tracking could mistake one sector for a completely different one, wiping or besieging the wrong location. Sector matching is now exact.
[*]🐛 [b]Removed a Second, Fake World-Eater:[/b] An old leftover spawner from early development could still trigger and drop a second "World Eater" into the galaxy, one with none of the real boss's mechanics and a bounty far bigger than it should have paid out. Only the real Doomsday Event World-Eater spawns now.
[*]🐛 [b]Fixed a Crash on Installing The Eclipse Bane:[/b] The unique reward for defeating the Vanguard boss could throw an error the moment you installed it, because of one broken stat entry. It now installs cleanly, with a bigger Shield Durability bonus in place of the broken one.
[*]🐛 [b]Eclipse Turret Loot Variety:[/b] Some sectors were quietly generating the exact same set of Eclipse turret drops as other, unrelated sectors, because of a coordinate math slip in the loot roller. Fixed, so turret variety across sectors is now properly random again.
[*]🐛 [b]World-Eater Enrage Music Fixed:[/b] The World-Eater has always had a second, more intense music track meant to kick in once it enters its Enrage phase at 35% health. It turns out that track never actually played, this whole time, in any fight. Fixed, so the fight now properly escalates musically once things get desperate.
[*]🐛 [b]Dark Sectors Now Actually Spawn:[/b] A flag meant to stop a sector from being re-checked was quietly getting set way too early, on almost every sector explorers passed through before the Eclipse even woke up. In practice this meant most sectors never got a real shot at becoming a Dark Sector once the crisis actually started. Fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Dark Sector Citadels No Longer Overlap or Teleport:[/b] Multiple Citadels spawning in the same Dark Sector could physically overlap each other, causing violent collision glitches, and they were also picking up a stray teleport-away ability that made no sense for a stationary fortress. Both fixed.
[*]🐛 [b]Eclipse Rift Spillage Could Trap Solo Players:[/b] The Rift Stabilizer that occasionally spawns during a personal Eclipse ambush was built using the same tool used for full Citadels, which meant it could also lock you in the sector until it was destroyed, something that was never supposed to happen for this hazard. You can now always leave the sector as intended; the shield-draining hazard itself is unchanged.
[*]🐛 [b]Various Under-the-Hood Fixes:[/b] Closed several smaller gaps found during a full audit of the mod's code, mostly around save/reload reliability.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.5.1[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.5.1 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch resolves some of the most elusive bugs reported by the community![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Linux Dedicated Server Fixes:[/b] Fixed a widespread issue where event scripts and campaigns were completely failing to load on Linux Dedicated Servers due to path-case sensitivity. The Eclipse and the Aegis campaign will now trigger flawlessly for multiplayer server hosts!
[*]🐛 [b]Script Crash Prevention:[/b] Fixed several hidden crashes where the engine would quietly fail when players or factions tried to pay for things (like Ascendancy Beacon upgrades) because of incorrect internal money assignments. The story missions and mega-structures are now much more stable.
[*]🐛 [b]Multiplayer UI & Interactivity:[/b] Repaired broken client-to-server communications across several custom UI windows. Buttons that were previously greyed out or completely unresponsive (such as the Ascendancy Beacon) will now work flawlessly in multiplayer!
[*]🐛 [b]Ascendancy Beacon Fixes:[/b] Fixed a nasty bug where trying to pay upkeep or activate the Ascendancy Beacon with ores (like Xanion or Avorion) would instantly crash the beacon's interface.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.5.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.5.0 🛠️ARCHITECTURE & OPTIMIZATION UPDATE!🛠️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ CORE ARCHITECTURE PATCH[/b]
[i]This minor update implements a total structural audit while bugfixing and tweaking the story campaign.[/i]

[b]🛠️ ARCHITECTURE & OPTIMIZATION[/b]
[list]
[*]⚡ [b]Global Wrapper Purge:[/b] Completely overhauled the internal C++ API wrapper structure across the codebase. Removed dozens of invalid legacy wrappers that were causing silent multiplayer linkage failures, aligning the entire mod with strict Avorion VFS constraints.
[*]⚡ [b]Namespace Alignment:[/b] All RPC registries and state persistence hooks have been rigorously audited and mapped directly to their correct namespace objects, guaranteeing flawless dedicated server synchronization.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Aegis Campaign:[/b] Fixed a severe structural logic flaw across the entire 5-part Aegis Story Campaign. Previously, Aegis would brute-force delete the mission scripts from your ship when handing out the next mission, which prevented them from officially logging as "Completed" in your quest log. All missions now gracefully detect when Aegis finishes speaking to you, allowing them to naturally call their completion logic and finish cleanly.
[*]🐛 [b]Callback Registrations:[/b] Patched the Singularity Detonation mechanics and several other entity scripts to correct target pointers that were missing their namespaces, restoring missing visual and mechanical effects.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.4.1[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.4.1 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets issues regarding visual effects![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Visual Desync & Server Crash Prevention:[/b] Fixed a critical server-side crash in `ca_worldeater_behavior.lua`, `ca_singularity_detonation.lua`, and `ca_anomaly_stash.lua` where the engine would attempt to execute `Sector():createExplosion()` or `createGlow()` directly on the server thread. All visual detonation logic has been strictly isolated and routed through `broadcastInvokeClientFunction`, ensuring massive cinematic explosions properly render for all clients in the sector without crashing the dedicated server.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.4.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.4.0 🛠️ARCHITECTURE & OPTIMIZATION UPDATE!🛠️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ CORE ARCHITECTURE PATCH[/b]
[i]This update implements Progressive Materialization to eliminate massive lag spikes during Eclipse expansions![/i]

[b]🛠️ ARCHITECTURE & OPTIMIZATION[/b]
[list]
[*]⚡ [b]Progressive Materialization (Lag Fix):[/b] Completely overhauled the [i]ca_expansion_manager[/i] API. When The Eclipse faction expands or annihilates a sector, they no longer force the server to physically load the sector into memory to generate stations or delete entities (which caused massive server stutters).
[*]⚡ [b]Lazy Loading API:[/b] Eclipse expansions and sector annihilations are now queued mathematically. When a player jumps into the affected sector, the game seamlessly intercepts the loading screen and instantly applies the changes. Zero stutter!
[*]⚡ [b]Threat Economy Safety:[/b] Added a 50ms CPU intercept check inside the Eclipse Threat Economy manager. This prevents the server from freezing when validating thousands of sectors against the Annihilation engine.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.3.1[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.3.1 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets a Matrix math crash![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Lore Anomalies:[/b] Fixed a C++ API logic exception (invalid type 'Matrix' expected 'vec3') when calculating randomized anomaly stash generation, preventing the lore databanks from appearing.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.3.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.3.0 ✨FEATURE & 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ MINOR EXPANSION PATCH[/b]
[i]Minor Features expansion![/i]

[b]✨FEATURES[/b]
[list]
[*]🔥 [b]Omni-Sensor Deep Scan:[/b] The Ascendant Omni-Sensor now automatically performs a deep scan upon entering a sector, printing the exact coordinates of any claimable asteroids or hidden stashes directly to your chat interface.
[*]🔥 [b]Slipstream Drift:[/b] Jumping into a sector with the Ascendant Slipstream Drive equipped now grants a massive +50% velocity boost for 10 seconds, simulating the momentum of exiting the hyperspace tunnel.
[*]🔥 [b]Void Drill Overclocking:[/b] The immense power draw of the Ascendant Void Drill now occasionally causes your ship to vent massive, harmless plasma bursts.
[*]🔥 [b]Anomaly Resurgence:[/b] When extracting databanks from a Lore Anomaly, there is now a 10% chance for the anomaly to resonate and spawn a secondary, smaller stash nearby containing bonus loot!
[/list]

[i]Version 1.2.5[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.2.5 🐛CRITICAL BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix directly addresses a severe crash that prevented deep-space anomalies from spawning correctly![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Lore Anomaly Crash Fixes:[/b] Fixed two critical server crashes when spawning deep-space corrupted databanks. The script was utilizing invalid and defunct logic to verify empty sectors and spawn wreckages, which would silently kill the sector thread. Anomalies will now properly detect empty sectors and natively spawn wreckages flawlessly!
[/list]

[i]Version 1.2.4[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.2.4 🐛CRITICAL BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix directly addresses a severe crash that prevented Aegis from spawning when players entered her rendezvous coordinates![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Aegis Spawn Crash:[/b] Fixed a severe legacy bug carried over through all campaign stages that caused the game backend to fail when attempting to spawn the Aegis Envoy ship. The mission will now correctly spawn Aegis when you arrive at the coordinates, allowing the questline to progress!
[/list]

[i]Version 1.2.3[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.2.3 🐛CRITICAL BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix directly addresses a severe race-condition crash that prevented Aegis from properly delivering her mail to players who immediately warped away after killing the Guardian![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Aegis Mail Trigger Crash:[/b] Fixed a critical hyperspace race-condition crash in `ca_story0`. If a player jumped to a new sector at the exact millisecond the 10-second Aegis delay timer elapsed, the mission would fail to grab the sector coordinates and silently crash, failing to deliver the rendezvous mail or objective. Replaced the static `Sector():getCoordinates()` API with the robust `player:getSectorCoordinates()` to ensure it safely resolves coordinates even during loading screens and hyperspace jumps.
[*]🐛 [b]Aegis Mission UI:[/b] Added the explicit `autoTrackMission = true` flag to the Aegis story mission. Now, the moment Aegis contacts the player and assigns the rendezvous coordinates, it will properly force the objective to appear on the player's right-hand HUD immediately, preventing players from missing the event.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.2.2[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.2.2 🐛BUGFIX & UI POLISH PATCH UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This small patch addresses legacy save compatibility and polishes the story mission user interface![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Aegis Legacy Save Compatibility:[/b] Fixed an issue where loading into an older save with the Wormhole Guardian already destroyed would trigger the Aegis encounter instantly without any narrative delay. Aegis will now properly wait a few moments before initiating contact.
[*]🐛 [b]Story Mission UI Polish & Softlocks:[/b] Safely patched all stages of the Cosmic Ascendancy narrative campaign. The missions are now explicitly marked as un-abandonable, preventing players from accidentally aborting the questline and soft-locking their playthrough. Also added missing descriptions and assigned the official story-mission icons for a cleaner mission log experience!
[*]🐛 [b]Dark Sector Premature Spawning:[/b] Fixed an issue where players exploring the deep core could stumble into Eclipse fleets and Dark Matter Fog before actually defeating the Wormhole Guardian to awaken them.
[/list]

