[i]Version 1.1.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v1.1.0 MASSIVE 🐛BUGFIX, ⚖️BALANCING, ⚙️ADJUSTMENTS AND ✨FEATURES PATCH UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This massive patch fixes severe server crashes, invalid API calls, API synchronization errors, and dangerous sector-wiping bugs while adjusting gameplay and adding in new features![/i]

[b]📦New Features[/b]
[list]
[*]✨ [b]World-Eater Grace Period:[/b] After defeating the Eclipse World-Eater (or surviving an execution), the entire galaxy is granted a 10 real-time hour Grace Period where the Doomsday timer is paused.
[*]✨ [b]Global Status Command:[/b] Added a new `/eclipsestatus` chat command available to all players. It allows players to check the remaining duration of the Citadel Suppression Field and the World-Eater Grace Period.
[/list]

[b]🖥️BALANCING[/b]
[list]
[*]⚖️ [b]Harbinger Re-Tune:[/b] Reduced the Shield Durability Multiplier on Eclipse Harbingers from +3750% to +1000% to ensure that the Eclipse World-Eater Raid Boss properly retains its crown as the supreme flagship of the Ascendant fleets.
[*]⚖️ [b]Living Relics True Power:[/b] Fixed tooltips and scaling for Ascendant Living Relics to ensure they grant the intended extreme stat bonuses.
[/list]

[b]🔧ADJUSTMENTS[/b]
[list]
[*]⚙️ [b]Server Save Bloat:[/b] Restructured Eclipse Stronghold generation to use localized scripts instead of global database flags, permanently preventing save-file bloat.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]World-Eater Crash:[/b] Fixed a fatal server crash during the doomsday sequence by correcting an invalid API call.
[*]🐛 [b]Ascendant Forge UI Failure:[/b] Fixed a catastrophic bug where station UI buttons failed to function. Exposed all UI hooks via global wrappers.
[*]🐛 [b]Gateway Entity Crash:[/b] Fixed a severe null-reference crash when scanning for hostile forces during siege events.
[*]🐛 [b]Gateway DPS Scaling:[/b] Replaced invalid `addMultiplyableBias` API call to properly grant Ascendant Guardians massive percentage DPS/Shield boosts.
[*]🐛 [b]Citadel Loot Monotony:[/b] Fixed identical turret drops from destroyed Citadels by properly seeding `SectorTurretGenerator`.
[*]🐛 [b]Payout Null-Crash:[/b] Replaced an unstable `player:receive()` API call in the World-Eater bounty loop with direct economy updates to prevent crashes.
[*]🐛 [b]Story Hyperspace Exploit:[/b] Patched a major exploit allowing players to skip boss fights by jumping to adjacent sectors. Missions now strictly validate player coordinates.
[*]🐛 [b]Monolith Math Desync:[/b] Fixed a fatal Lua crash caused by invalid matrix math during story anomaly generation.
[*]🐛 [b]Ascendant Overdrive UI:[/b] Fixed non-functional "Ascendant Overdrive" UI buttons and corrected its production capacity buff multiplier.
[*]🐛 [b]World-Eater Mechanics Breakdown:[/b] Fixed a catastrophic issue where the boss's core combat loop failed due to missing global lifecycle wrappers.
[*]🐛 [b]World-Eater DPS Scaling:[/b] Corrected invalid API usage to ensure the boss's damage scales properly with multiple players.
[*]🐛 [b]Ascendancy Beacon Failure:[/b] Fixed the beacon script failing to execute by exposing its hooks globally.
[*]🐛 [b]Beacon Toll Crash:[/b] Replaced a dangerous `owner:receive()` API call with direct assignment to prevent crashes during AI toll collection.
[*]🐛 [b]Siege Loot Generation Crash:[/b] Fixed a namespace call crash that terminated the script upon siege victory, restoring legendary rewards.
[*]🐛 [b]World-Eater Spawn Hang:[/b] Fixed a critical bug causing the Doomsday tracker and music to lock if the boss failed to spawn.
[*]🐛 [b]Siege Faction Desync:[/b] Fixed a server crash caused by treating raw integers as faction models and repaired siege defense rewards.
[*]🐛 [b]Boss Spawner Crash:[/b] Fixed a crash caused by calling a non-existent wormhole API and corrected turret generator arguments.
[*]🐛 [b]Ascendant Relic Buff Fixes:[/b] Audited all 8 endgame Living Relics to correctly grant percentage buffs via `addBaseMultiplier`.
[*]🐛 [b]Rift Hazard Engine Drain:[/b] Fixed a performance loop and integrated the shield drain with the native `inflictDamage` combat state API.
[*]🐛 [b]Script Injection Optimization:[/b] Added entity safeguards to prevent script injection into lightweight fighters, eliminating console spam.
[*]🐛 [b]Audio Hook Resolution:[/b] Integrated native `Music():playTrack()` implementations and fixed global wrapper RPC resolution.
[*]🐛 [b]Invasion Ghost Event:[/b] Fixed a crash during Eclipse invasions by including the native player library and adding hyperspace safety checks.
[*]🐛 [b]Campaign Desyncs:[/b] Fixed quest progression desyncs when entering sectors via gateway structures, and patched null-reference crashes.
[*]🐛 [b]Dark Sector Physics Collision:[/b] Fixed collision failures and physics lag by resolving fleet intersections during Dark Sector generation.
[*]🐛 [b]Alliance Territory Targeting:[/b] Updated World-Eater targeting to correctly protect player Alliance territories.
[*]🐛 [b]Eclipse Stronghold Generation:[/b] Fixed a missing callback hook error that prevented Strongholds from spawning.
[*]🐛 [b]Lore Anomaly Logic:[/b] Fixed a crash caused by invalid API calls and repaired library loading issues for the background event chain.
[*]🐛 [b]Singularity Turret Scope Crash:[/b] Fixed a crash when spawning Singularity ships by properly routing through the `Weapons` component.
[*]🐛 [b]World-Eater Summoning & Desync:[/b] Fixed state saving issues to prevent multiple simultaneous World-Eater spawns after reboots.
[*]🐛 [b]Singularity Detonation Engine Bug:[/b] Fixed a crash caused by missing imports and shifted damage to use the `inflictDamage` API.
[*]🐛 [b]Delayed Annihilation Instant-Death Trap:[/b] Fixed a bug where background sector annihilation would incorrectly wipe active player ships.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.0.5[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]🐛v1.0.5 BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch fixes silent errors and crashes during the Eclipse Awakening sequence![/i]

[*]🐛 [b]Flavor Text & Audio Silent Failure:[/b] Fixed a critical cross-script execution failure where the Eclipse Awakening UI banner and audio triggers were silently failing. The bridge functions in the player audio hook were encapsulated inside a namespace table and lacked global wrapper functions, which caused Avorion's `invokeFunction` and `invokeClientFunction` to silently fail when searching the script's global scope.

[*]🐛 [b]Eclipse Ghost Broadcasts:[/b] Fixed a bug where the Eclipse Doomsday broadcast would fire from a non-existent faction. The `eclipse_awakes.lua` script now explicitly instructs the engine to fully generate and register the Eclipse faction in the galaxy database at the exact moment the awakening timer hits zero, ensuring complete database stability for manager scripts.


[i]Version 1.0.4[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]🐛V1.0.4 BUGFIX & CODEX PATCH!📖[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX & CODEX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch fixes a silent crash during the Eclipse awakening sequence![/i]

[*]🐛 [b]Flavor Text & Audio Missing:[/b] Fixed a critical bug where the cinematic banner, music, and warning flavor text failed to display when the Wormhole Guardian was defeated. The global listener was using an invalid engine API (getPlayers() instead of getOnlinePlayers()), causing the script to crash immediately after detecting the Guardian's death. This resolves the silent failure during the Eclipse awakening sequence.

[*]🐛 [b]Missing Dark Fog Logic:[/b] Fixed a bug where jumping into a Dark Sector in the core attempted to load a non-existent weather script. Dark Sectors will now correctly spawn the Dark Matter Fog environmental hazard using the Vault API.

[*]📖 [b]Dark Matter Fog:[/b] Clarified the Codex entry for Dark Matter Fog. It does not deal passive damage-over-time; it solely imposes harsh debuffs on ship sensors and jump drives.

[i]Version 1.0.3[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]V1.0.3 🐛CRITICAL BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ CRITICAL HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch fixes a serious issue where The Eclipse would not properly load in![/i]
[*]🐛 [b]Eclipse Awakening Failure:[/b] Fixed a critical bug where The Eclipse failed to awaken after defeating the Wormhole Guardian. The core event scripts (`eclipse_awakes.lua` and `ca_expansion_manager.lua`) were missing the mandatory `data/scripts/` root path prefix when being attached to the `Galaxy()` singleton. Because the engine couldn't resolve the relative paths, it silently failed to load the scripts, causing the event listeners to never activate. The script initialization paths have been corrected and will retroactively detect the Guardian's death on existing saves.

[i]Version 1.0.2[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]V1.0.2 🐛BUGFIX, ⚖️BALANCING & ⚙️ADJUSTMENTS PATCH UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch fixes various bugs, balances many mechanics and numbers. Adjustments made to backend clockwork![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 Fixed a critical server/client synchronization "Bridge" crash where server-side scripts (World Eater, Eclipse) were calling client-only UI and Audio functions directly. Implemented bridge functions in `ca_boss_audio_hook.lua` to properly route UI banners and boss music triggers to the client.
[*]🐛 Fixed an issue in `eclipse_awakes.lua` where the 10-minute awakening timer was tied to `server.unpausedRuntime`, causing it to reset entirely if a dedicated server restarted during the countdown. It now properly persists using script localization parameters.
[*]🐛 Fixed an issue in `ca_world_eater_manager.lua` where the 3-hour cooldown timer was not being serialized during server shutdowns. The timer will now correctly persist across server restarts, ensuring World Eaters actually spawn.
[*]🐛 [b]Eclipse Awakening Trigger:[/b] Refactored the `eclipse_awakes.lua` trigger logic to seamlessly track Guardian kills via global `guardian_respawn_time` without polling players, fixing an edge-case where the event would fail to trigger if the killer disconnected immediately.
[/list]

[b]🖥️BALANCING[/b]
[list]
[*]⚖️ [b]Void Shields (Physical Mitigation):[/b] Reduced from 90% to 80%. This gives Physical weapons (Cannons, Bolters, Chainguns) a slight fighting chance, though Energy/Plasma/Antimatter remain highly recommended.
[*]⚖️ [b]Eclipse Citadel HP:[/b] Reduced base HP from 250,000,000 to 200,000,000 to make Citadel sieges slightly less of a slog.
[*]⚖️ [b]World Eater Spawn Timer:[/b] Increased the global spawn timer from 2-3 hours to 3-5 hours to make the encounter feel more like a rare galactic event.
[*]⚖️ [b]World Eater Doomsday Timer:[/b] Increased the Doomsday Sector Annihilation timer from 15 minutes to 20 minutes, giving players more time to rally a fleet and reach the location.
[*]⚖️ [b]Adaptive Armor (Defilers/Artillery):[/b] Reduced the heal-back amount while Adaptive Armor is active from 75% to 50%.
[*]⚖️ [b]Endgame Hazard Scaling:[/b] Converted all major Eclipse endgame hazards from flat-damage numbers to percentage-based scaling damage to ensure they remain lethal against ultra-lategame players with Ascendancy Beacons.
[*]⚖️ [b]Singularity Implosion:[/b] Converted from 250,000 flat true-damage to stripping 15% of a player's Max Hull.
[*]⚖️ [b]World Eater EMP Hazard:[/b] Converted from 1,000,000 flat Energy damage to 25% Max Hull damage (after stripping 100% shields).
[*]⚖️ [b]World Eater Breaker Laser:[/b] Converted from 5,000,000 flat Energy damage to a blast that deals 100% of Max Shields + 50% of Max Hull.
[*]⚖️ [b]World Eater Gravity Anomaly:[/b] Converted from 50,000 flat Physical DoT to 5% Max Hull per second.
[*]⚖️ [b]Eclipse Ambushes:[/b] Reduced the chance for the Eclipse to personally ambush players in their sector every 25-45 minutes from 60% down to 40%.
[*]⚖️ [b]Void Siphon Aura (Eclipse Command Ships):[/b] Reduced the massive heal-back conversion from draining players from 100% of damage drained down to 25%. The boss will no longer become an unkillable sponge if you bring a large fleet. Also reduced the aura radius from 15km to 10km to allow for better kiting.
[*]⚖️ [b]Dark Matter Blink (All Eclipse Ships):[/b] Increased the cooldown of the emergency teleport from 30 seconds to 45 seconds to reduce frustration when chasing ships with high-DPS builds.
[*]⚖️ [b]World-Eater Emergency Repairs:[/b] Reduced the Phase 50% Emergency Repair heal from 10% of Max Hull to 5% of Max Hull.
[/list]

[b]🔧ADJUSTMENTS[/b]
[list]
[*]⚙️ [b]Ambush Timer Persistence:[/b] Converted ambush invasion timers to use absolute real-time stamps (`Server().unpausedRuntime`) rather than tick-based accumulation, preventing desync from server lag.
[/list]

[i]Version 1.0.1[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]🐛V1.0.1 BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This small patch fixes an issue regarding the Rift Hazard anomaly![/i]
[*]🐛 Fixed an issue where the Rift Hazard anomaly would silently drain shields without notifying the player. Entering a hazard zone now immediately broadcasts a high-priority UI and chat warning. The Eclipse ships are unaffected by this anomaly.

[h1]⭐ [THE ASCENSION ERA] - Cosmic Ascendancy Official Release! ⭐[/h1]

[hr][/hr]

[h3]📡 Welcome to the Endgame![/h3]
The wait is over! Cosmic Ascendancy officially launches onto the Workshop as the ultimate capstone to the Cosmic Series. This expansion introduces a terrifying late-game crisis, god-tier crafting mechanics, and colossal megastructures that permanently alter your galaxy!

[b]⚠️ NEW SAVE FILE HARD REQUIRED ⚠️[/b]
Ascendancy relies on the massive architectural overhauls introduced across the Core 5 mods. You must start a new galaxy!

[hr][/hr]

💀 [b]THE ECLIPSE CRISIS & BOSS RAIDS[/b]
[list]
[*]🔥 [b]The Eclipse Crisis:[/b] Defeating the Wormhole Guardian triggers a galaxy-wide invasion! They permanently conquer sectors, deploy Lockdown Citadels, and unleash Rift Spillage hazards.
[*]☠️ [b]The World-Eater Boss Raid:[/b] An apocalyptic 5.9km Juggernaut! Features a 6-Phase Gauntlet with Quantum EMPs, Gravity Anomalies, Anchor Pylons, and Dark Matter Blinks! Summon it by jettisoning an Eclipse Datacore into space.
[*]🛡️ [b]Ancient Eclipse Mechanics:[/b] Eclipse vessels wield devastating abilities like Dark Matter Blinks, Ethereal Phase-Shifting, Adaptive Elemental Resistances, Void Siphon Auras, and Singularity Implosion death-blasts!
[*]⚔️ [b]The Fallen Empire Awakening:[/b] If The Eclipse annihilates 10 sectors, they enter a 'Fallen Empire' state, launching massive Crusade fleets to systematically hunt down and wipe out AI Faction Capitals.
[/list]

🏛️ [b]MEGASTRUCTURES & EMPIRE ECONOMY[/b]
[list]
[*]🏰 [b]The Ascendancy Beacon:[/b] Build a towering checkpoint that natively keeps your capital sector loaded 24/7! Upgrade it to Tier 5 to unlock permanent, account-wide multipliers to Hull, Shields, and Damage for all your ships.
[*]💰 [b]The Grand Toll:[/b] AI Factions and traders jumping into your Ascendant Capital are charged an entry tax. Warring factions pay a +50% premium for safe harbor! Taxes are stored safely and paid out as a massive lump sum every 45 minutes.
[*]🚨 [b]Capital Sieges:[/b] Defend your Ascendancy Beacon every 3 to 6 hours from devastating invasion fleets. If the beacon falls, your global buffs collapse!
[*]🏭 [b]Ascendant Overdrive:[/b] Feed 50 Ascendant Matter to any factory you own to activate Overdrive, instantly tripling (3.0x) its production capacity for 1 real-time hour!
[/list]

⚔️ [b]THE STELLAR FORGE & GOD-TIER ARSENAL[/b]
[list]
[*]⚒️ [b]The Stellar Forge:[/b] Extract Ascendant Matter from dead titans to asynchronously forge custom God-Tier weapons and Titan-Class Coaxial Lasers over 24 real-time hours.
[*]📈 [b]Wartime & Core Forging:[/b] Forging weapons near the Galactic Core during active wars yields exponential damage multipliers (up to 9.0x super-weapons)!
[*]♻️ [b]Ascendant Scrap System:[/b] Sacrifice Legendary or Exotic subsystems to boost crafting success. Failures yield 'Ascendant Scrap', which can be consumed to guarantee future crafts.
[*]💎 [b]Ascendant Subsystems (Living Relics):[/b] Equip game-breaking artifacts (War-Drive, Aegis Matrix, Swarm Nexus) that exponentially multiply their power (up to 7.5x) based on Core Proximity and active War Heat!
[*]🧠 [b]Ascendant Neural Implants:[/b] Wire your captain directly into the ship's core for massive bonuses to Jump Reach, Velocity, and Fighter Squadrons.
[*]💥 [b]Ascendant World-Breaker:[/b] A massive Titan-Class Coaxial weapon available in the Forge, delivering 250,000 baseline continuous damage to completely vaporize threats.
[/list]

🌌 [b]GALAXY EXPANSION & LORE[/b]
[list]
[*]📖 [b]Epic Story Campaign:[/b] Experience a 3-part narrative campaign to uncover the origins of the Eclipse, unlock the Stellar Forge, and claim The Eclipse Bane artifact!
[*]🗺️ [b]Faction AI 4x Expansion:[/b] AI Factions and Pirates now organically expand their borders, establish new stations in uncharted sectors, and utilize siege mechanics to conquer territory!
[*]🌑 [b]The Dark Sector:[/b] A terrifying new environmental hazard inside the Galactic Core. Jumping into un-generated sectors carries a 20% risk of dropping into a permanent Dark Matter Fog field crawling with Eclipse Juggernauts.
[*]📰 [b]Galactic Dread News:[/b] Server-wide breaking news broadcasts whenever The Eclipse annihilates a sector or you secure a Heroic Victory against a World-Eater.
[*]🤝 [b]Seamless Cross-Mod Synergy:[/b] Deeply integrated with Cosmic Vault (Global APIs), Cosmic War (Dynamic Tolls & Forge Multipliers), Cosmic Starfall (Eclipse Arsenal), and Cosmic Chronicles (Lore).
[*]🎵 [b]Custom OST Integration:[/b] The "Forge The Ascendant" custom soundtrack plays dynamically after the Wormhole Guardian's defeat.
[/list]

🛠️ [b]MULTIPLAYER STABILITY & OPTIMIZATION[/b]
[list]
[*]⚡ [b]Keep-Alive Engine:[/b] Custom background galaxy script natively handles 24/7 sector loading for the Beacon without dragging down server TPS.
[*]🔒 [b]Multiplayer RNG Sync:[/b] Built with deterministic Avorion `random()` engines to prevent massive multiplayer desyncs during Eclipse Vanguard invasions and procedural generation.
[*]🧠 [b]Memory Leak & Exploit Protection:[/b] Sealed volatile stat-stacking exploits on Living Relics. Safely handles Alliance inventory pulling for the Stellar Forge, preventing desyncs.
[*]🛡️ [b]Engine Crash Prevention:[/b] Hardened physics math to prevent gravity anomalies from crashing the server. Fixed multiple C++ index exceptions and native engine boundary crashes for flawless late-game stability.
[/list]


[b]Bug Fixes[/b]
- Fixed an architectural namespace violation in the World Eater Manager script where global wrapper functions were improperly defined, which could cause duplicate hook execution and VFS instability.
